  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "krein-domain",
      "verification": "formal",
      "statement": "Compare the completed blind readback and all actual declarations/definitions with the independent Krein contract and the exact original source definition. The claimed increment is a genuine complex L2 integral-representative domain with invariant closed-endpoint traces and class-independent -Second+c Value action, complex linearity, arbitrary MemLp2 Second construction/parameterization, actual derivatives and coordinate weak identities. Inspect all implicit binders and nonempty/domain witnesses. The two integral identities are model hypotheses, not assumptions of the desired derivative conclusions. The current increment claims only the integral representation and forward weak-H2 connection; reverse equivalence with separately defined classical weak H2, selfadjointness/positivity, inverse and Hc^s powers remain open. It must not be approved as the full original Krein theorem."
    },
    {
      "id": "krein-polynomial",
      "verification": "formal",
      "statement": "Compare the completed readback and exact root with independent polynomial/energy contracts and original p0,p1,p_even,p_odd family. Require genuine operator-domain membership for every real polynomial with the two original boundary residues zero, all original m>=2 without finite cutoffs, actual L2 action -p''+c p, and a proved Green integral giving first-variable-linear complex L2 energy. The identity is for all real c, hence includes source c>0; it does not assert positivity for arbitrary c. Energy covers real-polynomial complexifications; general complex full-domain energy, density and actual powers remain open. Verify this is a valid scoped increment without silently claiming full completeness."
    },
    {
      "id": "weighted-dd",
      "verification": "formal",
      "statement": "Compare the completed readback, model definitions and exact two-part root with independent weighted contracts and original density/ODE/mass excerpts. General norm bridge retains arbitrary positive bounded measurable density (no continuity or finite partition) and complex continuous values, with actual weighted L2 quotient membership and norm-squared equal to signed real weighted mass. Constant-DD construction must cover every real L>0, rho>0 and mathematical natural index n>=1, actual differential/integral solution, both DD endpoints, mass1 and genuine quotient norm1; lambda=omega^2 and k=n pi/L must be distinct. Verify positive parameters are satisfiable and eigenfunctions are nonzero. DN is only a boundary predicate in this increment. No full spectrum classification/order/completeness, general-density eigenfunction existence, B11 tail, spectral ratio or global extrema closure is claimed."
    }
  ],
